## ðŸ”¢ How the Grading System Works

### Grade â†’ Points Mapping (SPPU 10-Point Scale)

| Grade | Points | Meaning |
|-------|--------|---------|
| O | 10 | Outstanding |
| A+ | 9 | Excellent |
| A | 8 | Very Good |
| B+ | 7 | Good |
| B | 6 | Above Average |
| C | 5 | Average |
| P | 4 | Pass |
| F | 0 | Fail |

### Key Formulas

```
GP (Grade Points)  = Credits Ã— Grade Point Value
SGPA               = Total GP of Semester Ã· Total Credits Earned in Semester
CGPA               = Total GP of All Semesters Ã· Total Credits Earned Across All Semesters
```

> [!IMPORTANT]
> High-credit subjects (3 credits) have a **disproportionate impact** on SGPA/CGPA.  
> A P(4) in a 3-credit subject = 12 GP. A B+(7) would've been 21 GP. That's **9 GP lost** from one subject.

